        "subject": "LU-20335 misc: remove __GFP_HIGHMEM from __vmalloc() callers",
        "message": "LU-20335 misc: remove __GFP_HIGHMEM from __vmalloc() callers\n\nLinux commit 07003531e037 (\"mm/vmalloc: warn on invalid vmalloc gfp\nflags\") enforces the set of gfp flags the vmalloc family accepts. Any\nunsupported flag now triggers a warning and is stripped:\n\n    +static gfp_t vmalloc_fix_flags(gfp_t flags)\n    +{\n    +\tgfp_t invalid_mask = flags & ~GFP_VMALLOC_SUPPORTED;\n    +\n    +\tflags &= GFP_VMALLOC_SUPPORTED;\n    +\tWARN_ONCE(1, \"Unexpected gfp: %#x (%pGg). Fixing up to gfp: %#x (%pGg). Fix your code!\\n\",\n    +\t\t  invalid_mask, &invalid_mask, flags, &flags);\n    +\treturn flags;\n    +}\n\n__GFP_HIGHMEM is not part of GFP_VMALLOC_SUPPORTED, so update various\n__vmalloc() callers to stop passing this flag. __vmalloc will use it\nautomatically since 19809c2da28a (\"mm, vmalloc: use __GFP_HIGHMEM\nimplicitly\") which is present in all kernels (v4.12+) that Lustre\nsupports.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: 635421641bfa (\"LU-5349 include: use __vmalloc() to avoid __GFP_FS default\")\nSigned-off-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I917d4c8a27c9754b5393fe1bd9c84a09ae2d74c9\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
